#!/usr/bin/env node
/**
 * Get a quotation, the new way: CAR FIRST, in 4 steps (confirmed with the person via mockup). Run patch-quote-real-car first.
 *   1 the car: My Garage, or Brand > Model > Year > Version from the catalogue (never typed), "Save it to My Garage"; VIN optional;
 *   2 who it is for: a raised list (icons, light and dark), the name, the policy number for an insurer, the police / Najm report and the plate (optional);
 *   3 the parts: the shop filtered to that exact car and version, so every part shown FITS it (the sellers' fitment); search or a section; + adds it to the
 *     quotation. Parts brought from the basket are checked too: one that does not fit must be removed. "Can't find a part?" opens a part request;
 *   4 who pays and the delivery address. Then the quotation: the server checks the car AND that every part fits it again.
 * Starts from a new "Get a quotation" icon at the top of Home, "+ New quotation" in My quotations, or the basket's button (with the ticked parts).
 * On an open quotation, "Order these parts" puts its parts in the basket (only they ticked) to pay as any order, at today's prices.
 * Buyer app (EN + AR) and the server. The website's quotation page follows in its own patch.
 *
 *   node scripts/patch-quote-steps.js            dry run
 *   node scripts/patch-quote-steps.js --write    applies it (each changed file is saved as <file>.before-patch-quote-steps first)
 * Then: API: cd services\\api ; npm run dev (no migration) · buyer app: R
 *
 * A file that is not as this patch expects is NOT changed. Windows (CRLF) line endings are handled. Running it twice is harmless.
 */
